@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
title Angular Authentication Routes and Approved Future Navigation
left to right direction
rectangle "Login /login" as Login
rectangle "layouts/dashboard-layout\nDashboardLayout" as Shell
rectangle "Customer routes" {
  rectangle "Transactions list" as T
  rectangle "Transaction detail" as TD
  rectangle "Submit dispute" as F
  rectangle "Dispute history" as H
  rectangle "Customer dispute detail" as HD
}
rectangle "Agent routes" {
  rectangle "Unassigned / Mine / All" as Q
  rectangle "Agent case detail" as AD
  rectangle "Claim / Release / Resolve" as ACT
}
rectangle "Customer landing /customer" as CL
rectangle "Agent landing /agent" as AL
rectangle "Access denied" as Denied
rectangle "Session check retry" as Retry
Login --> Shell : Verified server identity + refreshed CSRF
Shell --> CL : CUSTOMER
Shell --> AL : AGENT
Shell --> Login : Confirmed logout / expiry
Shell --> Denied : Wrong role
Login --> Retry : Unavailable initialization
CL ..> T : Future customer feature
AL ..> Q : Future agent feature
T --> TD : Select transaction
TD --> F : Eligible transaction
TD --> HD : Already disputed
F --> HD : Created successfully
T --> H : My Disputes
H --> HD : Open case
Q --> AD : Select case
AD --> ACT : Authorized action
ACT --> AD : Refresh status
note bottom
Desktop: full navigation and dense tables.
Mobile: collapsed navigation and stacked rows.
Use Nunito Sans, #2F70EF buttons, own Lucide icons.
Backend enforces authorization independently.
Startup: bootstrap then identity; no protected content while unresolved.
Return URLs allow only existing role landing routes.
Ambiguous logout hides content and offers explicit retry.
Collection controls: search + filters + sorting + 1-based pages.
Envelope success status is distinct from domain status.
end note
@enduml
